          }
        ],
        "created": "2025-09-25T18:35:28+00:00",
        "updated": "2025-09-25T18:35:28+00:00",
        "name": "Lotus",
        "scenario": "general.botanicExample",
        "scientificName": "N. nucifera",
        "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelumbo_nucifera",
        "description": "Nelumbo nucifera, also known as Padma (Sanskrit: \\\\u092a\\\\u0926\\\\u094d\\\\u092e, romanized: Padm\\\\u0101, lit.\\\\u2009'Lotus') or Kamala (Sanskrit: \\\\u0915\\\\u092e\\\\u0932, lit. 'Lotus'), sacred lotus, pink lotus, Indian lotus,[1] or simply lotus, is one of two extant species of aquatic plant in the family Nelumbonaceae. It is sometimes colloquially called a water lily, though this more often refers to members of the family Nymphaeaceae.[2] The lotus belongs in the order Proteales."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Plant",
      "id": "74023bac-88ea-4031-b4a5-68d861ea2e91",
      "data": {
        "images": [
          {
            "description": "Saucer Magnolia -- Magnolia × soulangeana 'Rustica Rubra' found in Houston, Texas",
            "imageLinkFull": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Saucer_Magnolia_--_Magnolia_%C3%97_soulangeana.jpg",
            "imageLinkThumbnail": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Saucer_Magnolia_--_Magnolia_%C3%97_soulangeana.jpg/960px-Saucer_Magnolia_--_Magnolia_%C3%97_soulangeana.jpg",
            "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Saucer_Magnolia_--_Magnolia_%C3%97_soulangeana.jpg"
          },
          {
            "description": "Yulan Magnolia (Magnolia denudata)",
            "imageLinkFull": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/Yulan_1.JPG",
            "imageLinkThumbnail": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/Yulan_1.JPG",
            "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Yulan_1.JPG"
          }
        ],
        "created": "2025-09-25T18:35:28+00:00",
        "updated": "2025-09-25T18:35:28+00:00",
        "name": "Magnolia",
        "scenario": "general.botanicExample",
        "scientificName": "M. denudata",
        "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnolia_denudata",
        "description": "Magnolia denudata, the lilytree[2] or Yulan magnolia (simplified Chinese: \\\\u7389\\\\u5170\\\\u82b1; traditional Chinese: \\\\u7389\\\\u862d\\\\u82b1; pinyin: y\\\\u00f9l\\\\u00e1nhu\\\\u0101; lit. 'jade orchid/lily'), is native to central and eastern China.[3] It has been cultivated in Chinese Buddhist temple gardens since 600 AD. Its flowers were regarded as a symbol of purity in the Tang dynasty and it was planted in the grounds of the emperor's palace. It is the official city flower of Shanghai."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Plant",
      "id": "de004523-5165-4f10-872b-92eb9637a5d1",
      "data": {
